@@ -36,0 +37,4 @@ Synthetic-only additions: append-only tenant switch reasons/revisions, actor mem
+
+## ENT-10a2 synthetic inbound deactivation
+
+Local inbound only: the in-process test provider submits an opaque subject and UUID message id at the connection's route. The restricted identity service hashes the unchanged subject and canonical message; the new immutable company-scoped record holds hashes, identifiers, outcome, counts and server time. No address, raw subject, bearer or seed is stored, audited or logged. Revocation and the identifier/hash-only company audit append share one transaction. Caller proof derives from JOBGUARD_SCIM_SYNTHETIC_SEED (no default, no persisted value); every unavailable/unapproved route falls back to deny. Processing is in the application process; storage is configured synthetic PostgreSQL; logs are redacted; fixtures are disposable; no training, live backup approval or outbound provider flow. Gate status synthetic-only: only JOBGUARD_ENV synthetic_demo and database jobguard_synthetic_demo; D04/G5 live provider evidence remains HELD. See [scim-deactivation-v1.md](../contracts/scim-deactivation-v1.md) for refusal, replay, owner protection and invitation limits.
diff --git a/packages/db/MIGRATIONS.md b/packages/db/MIGRATIONS.md
index 9016bdc..51343d2 100644
--- a/packages/db/MIGRATIONS.md
+++ b/packages/db/MIGRATIONS.md
@@ -881,0 +882,6 @@ append-only facts to roll back. The integrator owns the BUILD_PLAN §12.2 ledger
+
+## 0137 — synthetic SCIM deactivation (ENT-10a2)
+
+Adds only `identity.scim_event` (immutable, tenant-qualified, FORCE RLS, no application table privileges) and `identity.scim_deactivate(uuid,jsonb)` (restricted identity EXECUTE only; SECURITY DEFINER with pg_catalog search path). No object from 0111, 0120 or 0129 altered or restated; no backfill; no existing row changed by the migration. No column, index, constraint, policy, trigger or grant added to any existing table. PostgreSQL creates the internal foreign-key enforcement triggers automatically as part of the new table's constraints.
+
+The governed repository transaction writes existing one-way membership/session revocation facts, grant revocations and the record, then appends the audit event last. This is the first product code to set app.membership.revoked_at. Existing request gates remain unchanged. Synthetic database only, replay once, owner protected, no reactivation. Roll forward for any repair; removing the new objects is permissible only before any message has been accepted. Accepted history and revocation facts must never be cleared by rollback. Upgrade proof snapshots populated named columns, full types and primary-key identities before this migration, verifies this migration alone, then applies later migrations twice. Database tests are NOT RUN (sandbox cannot start PostgreSQL / a browser).
